Barrie,

I was wrong about the jobs. We are still going to need to pull the department name. Sorry, everyone is still figuring the system out.

Jobs should be from this page https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/ but for the specific position.

Here is an example:
University Policy Manager - Moscow, Idaho, United States<https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/university-policy-manager-moscow-idaho-united-states>


Here is the text we would need to pull (highlighted). We would not want the "749-PROV" type text each one has.

Same as before, we would only run location if it wasn't listed as Moscow.

Appointment Information
Working Title: University Policy Manager
Division/College: 3976-PROV Provost Exec VP Area
Department: 749-PROV Provost Office
Location: Moscow



From: Bauer, Joy (jbauer@uidaho.edu)
Sent: Tuesday, November 3, 2026 1:44 PM
To: Robison, Barrie (brobison@uidaho.edu) <brobison@uidaho.edu>; Addington, Colin (caddington@uidaho.edu) <caddington@uidaho.edu>
Subject: UCM AI tool and Jobs

Barrie and Colin,

I just remembered one thing. With the new PageUp job system which replaced People Admin, we no longer need to get the tool to check the department field. Instead, we only need to use the "Working title" which is at the top and includes the title and department.

Examples:

Appointment Information
Working Title: Associate Vice President of Principal Giving, UI Foundation

Preview job ad - PageUp People<https://uidaho.dc4.pageuppeople.com/v5.3/provider/previewJob/PreviewJob.aspx?lJobSourceID=2890>


Joy Bauer, '98
Internal Content Coordinator
University Communications and Marketing
jbauer@uidaho.edu<mailto:jbauer@uidaho.edu>

[University of Idaho]



